## Detailed Changes

### 1. Backend Layer

#### [MODIFY] [backend/src/services/captain.service.ts](file:///e:/Main-Projects/rapido/backend/src/services/captain.service.ts)
- Update `getCaptainScheduledRides`:
  - Broaden `where.status` to include **both** `RideStatus.SCHEDULED` and `RideStatus.SEARCHING` (for unassigned scheduled rides whose `scheduledAt` is within the dispatch window).
  - This guarantees that rides in the 15-minute dispatch window do NOT disappear from the Captain's Scheduled view.
- Add `getCaptainActiveRequest(userId: string)`:
  - Check if the captain is `AVAILABLE`.
  - Look for an active `SEARCHING` ride that matches:
    - Unassigned (`captainId: null`).
    - Scheduled pickup within the active dispatch window (or immediate ride).
    - Captain has not rejected it (`rejections: { none: { captain: { userId } } }`).
    - Vehicle type matches captain's vehicle.
  - Returns the pending ride request so the Cockpit can display it reliably on load and poll.

#### [MODIFY] [backend/src/controllers/captain.controller.ts](file:///e:/Main-Projects/rapido/backend/src/controllers/captain.controller.ts)
- Add `getActiveRequest`:
  - Calls `getCaptainActiveRequest(userId)`.
  - Returns `{ success: true, data: activeRequest }`.

#### [MODIFY] [backend/src/routes/captain.routes.ts](file:///e:/Main-Projects/rapido/backend/src/routes/captain.routes.ts)
- Add route `GET /captains/active-request` pointing to `getActiveRequest`.

#### [MODIFY] [backend/src/services/matching.service.ts](file:///e:/Main-Projects/rapido/backend/src/services/matching.service.ts)
- In `getNearbyCaptains`:
  - Enhance fallback for local/dev environment or testing: if Redis GEO set is empty or captain GPS hasn't emitted within 5 minutes, fallback to finding online captains with `status: AVAILABLE` in PostgreSQL so captains testing in browser Cockpit always receive the incoming dispatch.

#### [MODIFY] [backend/src/services/ride.service.ts](file:///e:/Main-Projects/rapido/backend/src/services/ride.service.ts)
- In `startMatchingForRide`:
  - Pass full details in `io.to('captain:...').emit('ride:new', { ... })`: include `pickupAddress`, `pickupName`, `destinationAddress`, `destinationName`, `scheduledAt`, and `vehicleType`.
  - Adjust `cancelIfNoAssignment` timeout for scheduled rides:
    - Instead of a hardcoded 2 minutes, allow scheduled rides to remain searching until closer to pickup (e.g. 10 minutes or until `scheduledAt`), with periodic re-broadcast to available captains every 30-45s.

#### [MODIFY] [backend/src/jobs/rideQueue.ts](file:///e:/Main-Projects/rapido/backend/src/jobs/rideQueue.ts)
- In `reconciliation` job:
  - Ensure scheduled rides within 15 minutes of departure that are still `SCHEDULED` are immediately transitioned and dispatched to captains, safeguarding against any delayed BullMQ edge cases.

